WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:04.240
it.

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.560
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.530
For this prep, you'll need a few items, all available over the counter, no

5
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.000
prescription needed.

6
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.680
You'll need one 238 gram bottle of MiraLAX powder, 2 to 4 Dulcolax laxative

7
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.360
tablets,

8
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.040
and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink like Gatorade Propel or Crystal Light.

9
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:30.640
That's usually two 32-ounce bottles. If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade

10
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.200
G2.

11
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.160
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

12
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.360
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.160
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

14
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.520
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

15
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.300
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

16
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:55.760
sports drink.

17
00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.600
Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

18
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.690
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like. Keeping it cold makes it

19
00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.480
easier to drink.

20
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.160
Now for part one, the evening before your procedure.

21
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.640
At 5 p.m., take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

22
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.400
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four.

23
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.720
Follow their guidance on the specific amount.

24
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.280
At 6 p.m., you'll start drinking the first half of the solution.

25
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.960
That's 32 ounces. Drink an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half

26
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:29.520
is gone.

27
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.360
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish.

28
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.640
For part two, six hours before your colonoscopy, you'll drink the second half,

29
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:44.640
which is another 32 ounces. Drink this at the same pace, an eight ounce glass

30
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.840
every 15 minutes.

31
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:49.960
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

32
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:50.720
procedure.

33
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.320
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

34
00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.040
directed,

35
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.360
even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough,

36
00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.920
but finishing the entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during your

37
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:05.680
procedure.

38
00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.690
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

39
00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.600
of us wants that.

40
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.080
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

41
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.800
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

42
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.200
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

43
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.680
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

44
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.310
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

45
00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.320
hydrated.

46
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.540
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

47
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.320
to help.
